{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "id": "kukhnya-s01e03-scene-04",
 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Опасный разговор  (A Dangerous Conversation)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "max": "Макс",
  "vadim": "Вадим"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "A rough-looking man stops Max outside Claude Monet. His name is Vadim, he is a prosecutor, and he wants to know who Vika is seeing these days. Max is not enjoying this. Here's the conversation in Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Слышь, малой, есть разговор.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Что вам нужно?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Тут у вас работает Вика.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Виктория Сергеевна.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "С кем она тут встречается?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Ну, почему молчим?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Почему я должен отвечать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Не хочешь отвечать здесь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Ответишь у меня в прокуратуре.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Ты меня понял?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Понял, всё понял.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Она ни с кем не встречается.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Ну, смотри у меня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Надо срочно предупредить всех.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's go through the threat.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Слышь, малой, есть разговор.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Listen, kid, I want to talk.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Слышь,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is street speech, built from the word for \"do you hear\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "малой,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " meaning kid, is built from the word for \"small\", and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "есть разговор.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to \"there is a conversation\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Что вам нужно?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What do you need?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Что вам нужно?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to \"what to you needed?\". Max uses ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "вам",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the polite word for \"you\", with a stranger.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Тут у вас работает Вика.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Vika works here with you.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "у вас",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to \"at you\", meaning \"at your place\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Тут",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is an everyday word for \"here\", and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "работает",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to \"works\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Виктория Сергеевна.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Viktoria Sergeyevna.' A first name plus the father's name, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Сергеевна.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning daughter of Sergey, built from the name Sergey, is the formal way to name an adult.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "С кем она тут встречается?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Who is she seeing here?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "встречается?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to \"meets with\", which is the normal way to say you're dating someone. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "С кем",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to \"with whom\", built from the word for \"who\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Ну, почему молчим?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well, why are we silent?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "молчим?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to \"we are silent\", built from the action word for \"to be silent\". Vadim says \"we\" when he means \"you\", the scolding \"we\" used on children.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Почему я должен отвечать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Why should I answer?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "должен",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to \"should\", and has a man's ending. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "отвечать?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the action word for \"to answer\", is built from the naming word for \"an answer\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Не хочешь отвечать здесь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Don't want to answer here?' Vadim has called Max the informal \"you\" from his first word, and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "хочешь",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the matching form of the word for \"want\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "здесь?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to \"here\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Ответишь у меня в прокуратуре.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You'll answer in my prosecutor's office.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Ответишь",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the finished action word, so it translates to \"you will answer\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "у меня в прокуратуре.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to \"at me in the prosecutor's office\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Ты меня понял?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Did you understand me?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Ты меня понял?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to \"you me understood?\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "понял?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " has a man's ending because Max is a man.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Понял, всё понял.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Understood, understood everything.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Понял, всё понял.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " repeats the same word and adds ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "всё",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the word for \"everything\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Она ни с кем не встречается.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'She is not seeing anyone.' The pieces of the word for \"nobody\" come apart around the word for \"with\", to make ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "ни с кем",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ". Then ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "не",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " follows, so the double negative has a connecting word wedged inside it.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Ну, смотри у меня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well, you watch yourself.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "смотри у меня.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to \"look, at me\", meaning \"careful, or you'll answer to me\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "смотри",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the informal command built from the action word for \"to look\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Надо срочно предупредить всех.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Must urgently warn everyone.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Надо",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to a one-word \"must\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "предупредить",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to \"to warn\", and the word for \"everyone\" becomes ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "всех.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " as the target of the action. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Слышь, малой, есть разговор.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Что вам нужно?",
   "gap": 0.5
